## Getting Started w/ R
Download, install, and open RStudio.

## Learn R
Install and use swirl within RStudio to learn R.

## R Package vs. Library
In R, a package is a collection of R functions, data and compiled code. The location where the packages are stored is called the library. If there is a particular functionality that you require, you can download the package from the appropriate site and it will be stored in your library.
Source: <https://stackoverflow.com/questions/26900228/what-is-the-difference-between-a-library-and-a-package-in-r/>

## .Rmd Files
You "Knit" a .Rmd file.

## Find R Executable
Run in RStudio:
$ file.path(R.home("bin"), "Rscript.exe")

## Check for R Packages
$ install.packages('rmarkdown')
$ system.file(package = "rmarkdown")
$ rmarkdown::pandoc_available()
$ rmarkdown::find_pandoc()
$ rmarkdown::find_pandoc(cache = FALSE)
$ Sys.getenv("RSTUDIO_PANDOC")
$ getwd()
$ Sys.which("pandoc")

## Check if File or Folder Exists
$ dir.exists("folder_name") # folder name
$ file.exists("folder_name/filename.R") # filename
$ list.files("folder_name", full.names = TRUE)